What the AI does
AI in the world of supply chain can be better used for fulfillment, replenishment, and AI can be better used to project that products are going to be needed in future. AI can also be used to identify possible substitutions. AI also in project management can be used to better ensure that all tasks that need to be completed get completed. AI can be used as a way to hollistcally view how effecient certain individuals are at getting done tasks. AI can be used in a number of ways to ensure that all parts of project get done right.  

What data it uses
AI uses all data provided to it. In supply chain it would be all the data of the amounts of items, how frequently they are purchased. In project management, AI would use all data involving time to completion, resources used in completion. This one is a little harder for AI to monitor. AI can only use what has been provided to it. 
What business problem it solves
AI in supply chain can solve several problems. It can notice minor shifts in the supply chain that maybe someone who works in supply chain might not notice. AI can potentially solve issues like over-ordering, or under-ordering. AI in project managemnrt can solve problems where people aren't doign their jobs and making sure that projects happen in most efficient way. 
Who benefits
AI benefits larger business and their supply chain. It allows for them to cut down on the overall amount of people needed to run a supply chain. This could also allow them to expand their operations because they can have more employees that can be much more effecient. 
What could go wrong
AI could make a lot of possible mistakes with supply chain management. It could over-order products and cost the business tens of thousands of dollars. AI could also make massive assumptions and without thorough guidance could make a set of decisions that are not in the businesses best interests. AI can also not be a physical verification tool for products. 
